{"text": "PAUL D. ECHELARD\n\n1167 Hillsboro Mile @ Hillsboro Beach, Florida 33062 @ (561) 350-1858 e paulechelard@mac.com\n\nSUMMARY\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014____[[\"[{\u2014_______\u2014__\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nA visionary and strategic health system leader and hospital CEO with deep experience and success in all\naspects of for profit and not for profit healthcare management including: Future Vision, Compliance, A\nCulture of Accountability and Success, and Operational and Financial excellence. A savvy business leader,\nchallenges all associates to provide excellent clinical outcomes in the most cost effective manner. A\ncharismatic \u201cchange agent\u201d and \u201cmentor\u201d who develops leadership teams to transform and lead\nhealthcare organizations through challenging times of healthcare reform and the quest to continually\nposition the organization for the future.\n\nBEX PRE REIN CE Mm\n\nBROWARD HEALTH, Fort Lauderdale, Florida\nSenior Vice President, Chief Operating Officer, 2011-2015\n\nOversaw daily clinical and financial operations for tenth largest public healthcare system in United States. Functioned as\nkey leader in developing strategic business plans for each business unit throughout healthcare system.\n\nVISION:\n\nLed Ambulatory Strategy for healthcare system that included development and operationalizing Urgent Care\nCenters, diagnostic services and community healthcare centers. Created a plan for the development of future\n\"signature\" ambulatory centers in Broward County.\n\nKey leader in the development of Strategic Business Plans with measurable objectives for each business unit\nthroughout healthcare system. Generated growth in key clinical services.\n\nLed process to develop Master Campus Plans for each business unit within healthcare system which resulted in\nbetter utilization of real estate and properties to align with business, growth and operational needs. Included\nbuying/selling key properties, and consolidating services to position healthcare system for future development.\n\nPlanned and relocated 175 employees to a new Corporate Headquarters in a strategically centralized location.\n\nOPERATIONS/FINANCE:\n\nEstablished Hospitalist and Intensivist Programs in key facilities that resulted in improved patient care and clinical\noutcomes, increased patient satisfaction, financial and operational efficiency and grew patient volumes.\n\nEstablished culture of meeting budget expectations within each business unit which resulted in system exceeding\nbudget, growth and financial expectations during each year.\n\nLed multiple construction projects totaling approximately $150 million that included construction of new patient\ncare sites, renovation of patient care sites and meeting code requirements for all healthcare facilities. Approved\nfuture projects in process of development totaling approximately $500 million.\n\nChaired ICD-10 initiative to prepare system for compliance with new coding and billing system. Will affect all\nbilling for nearly $1 billion of patient care services\n\nCOMPLIANCE:\n\nEstablished process for individual physician contracts to ensure compliance with governmental regulations and business\npractices. Put in place approximately 1200 contracts that were well documented, timely and met all regulatory\nrequirements.\n\nEducated system executives on compliance requirements that has led to a consistent and compliant process that\nis well documented.",
